## Usage

```
make odo_gen
./odo_gen <epoch_seed> <throughput> [module_prefix] > encrypt.v
```

`epoch_seed` is the OdoCrypt epoch key: `ntime - ntime % 864000` on mainnet
(864000s = 10 days), where `ntime` is ideally the current chain tip's block
time (not just wall clock, though they track closely except right at a
10-day boundary).

For a drop-in replacement of `hdl/odocrypt/encrypt.v` (the shared core the
real board builds use — see hardware/qmtech-kintex7/ and hardware/zynq/),
use `throughput=4` and `module_prefix=encrypt_4` — that matches the module
names already in that file (`encrypt_4pre_mix`, `encrypt_4sbox_large0`,
...), which is how it was generated in the first place. Do NOT regenerate
`exmaples/odocrypt/fpga/src/hdl/encrypt.v` this way — that copy is the
original upstream/vendor example, deliberately left at its original epoch
so it stays paired with `exmaples/odocrypt/test/`'s matching test vectors.
